window.AGENT_CARDS = [{"n":0.1,"ti":"Python for Agent Code","f":"p1-python-for-agents.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"ollama-python built a schema from level: Literal[\"INFO\", \"WARN\", \"ERROR\"] = \"ERROR\" . What did the model receive for level ?","o":["An enum of the three values, optional","An enum of the three values, required","A plain string, marked required","Nothing: the parameter was dropped"],"a":2,"w":"The allowed values were lost and the default was ignored; the model then sent \"error\", \"warning\", \"critical\" and so on."},{"n":0.1,"ti":"Python for Agent Code","f":"p1-python-for-agents.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Eight requests to qwen3:14b took 2.94 s one at a time and 2.91 s with asyncio.gather . Why no gain?","o":["gather runs coroutines one after another","The Ollama server handled one request at a time and queued the rest","The GPU was too slow","The prompts were too short"],"a":1,"w":"The default OLLAMA_NUM_PARALLEL is 1. The same code made eight HTTP calls 8× faster."},{"n":0.1,"ti":"Python for Agent Code","f":"p1-python-for-agents.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Four parallel slots with 16k context each made the eight requests slower than one slot. Why?","o":["Python's GIL blocked the requests","The prompts were truncated","The semaphore limit was too low","Each slot reserves its own context memory, so the model no longer fitted on the GPU and part ran on the CPU"],"a":3,"w":"28% of the model ran on the CPU. With 4k per slot it stayed on the GPU and took 1.21 s."},{"n":0.1,"ti":"Python for Agent Code","f":"p1-python-for-agents.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"A command started with shell=True and a 2-second timeout kept the caller waiting for more than 10 seconds. What fixes it?","o":["Kill the whole process tree on timeout, and avoid the shell","A longer timeout","Reading stdout before stderr","Running it with asyncio"],"a":0,"w":"The timeout killed only the shell; the child held the pipe open. Killing the tree ended it in 2.62 s."},{"n":0.1,"ti":"Python for Agent Code","f":"p1-python-for-agents.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Which record lets you rerun a puzzling agent step exactly?","o":["The final answer and the date","The user's question and the model name","Messages, tool schemas, model digest, server version and options such as temperature, seed and num_ctx","A screenshot of the output"],"a":2,"w":"Any of those can change what the model sees or does."},{"n":0.2,"ti":"Chat Messages, Roles & Turns","f":"p2-chat-messages-and-roles.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Asked \"And what was the value?\" with no earlier messages, the model asked which metric was meant. Why?","o":["The server's cache expired","Temperature was 0","The tool was not offered","The model only sees the messages in the request, and none of the earlier turns were sent"],"a":3,"w":"Models are stateless; the transcript you send is all they know."},{"n":0.2,"ti":"Chat Messages, Roles & Turns","f":"p2-chat-messages-and-roles.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"How does Ollama's template for qwen3 send a tool result to the model?","o":["As a separate tool turn tagged with the tool's name","As a user turn wrapped in <tool_response> tags, without the tool's name","Inside the system message","As an assistant message"],"a":1,"w":"Which is why results are matched to calls only by order unless the text says what it is."},{"n":0.2,"ti":"Chat Messages, Roles & Turns","f":"p2-chat-messages-and-roles.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Two parallel results came back in the opposite order, as bare percentages. What happened in the 20 comparisons?","o":["Every answer attributed the values to the wrong hosts","The model asked to call the tools again","Half were right by chance","The model refused to answer"],"a":0,"w":"0 of 20 right. Labelling each value with its host made all 20 right in the same order."},{"n":0.2,"ti":"Chat Messages, Roles & Turns","f":"p2-chat-messages-and-roles.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"One question cost 22 prompt tokens with no tools and 5,954 with fifty. When is that cost paid?","o":["Once, when the tools are registered","Only when a tool is called","On every request that includes the tools, so on every agent step","Never: tool definitions are free"],"a":2,"w":"Definitions are rendered into the system turn of every request."},{"n":0.2,"ti":"Chat Messages, Roles & Turns","f":"p2-chat-messages-and-roles.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"The transcript ended with the assistant's tool call and no result. What did the model return?","o":["The same tool call again","An error from the server","An empty reply, because the request was treated as a continuation of the assistant's turn","A guessed value"],"a":2,"w":"20 of 20 were empty. A loop that treats \"no tool calls\" as finished would return nothing."},{"n":0.3,"ti":"JSON & JSON Schema","f":"p3-json-and-json-schema.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"With a schema giving only property types, how many of 30 calls were valid?","o":["All 30","None","About half","27"],"a":1,"w":"The model invented metric names, severities and formats. With the full schema, 27 were valid."},{"n":0.3,"ti":"JSON & JSON Schema","f":"p3-json-and-json-schema.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"What does additionalProperties: false protect against?","o":["Missing required fields","Values outside an enum","Strings in number fields","Invented or misspelt fields that would otherwise be ignored silently"],"a":3,"w":"Without it, dry_run sent to a tool expecting dryRun just disappears."},{"n":0.3,"ti":"JSON & JSON Schema","f":"p3-json-and-json-schema.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"A user asked for a memory alert; the call used disk_used_pct and passed validation. What does this show?","o":["Validation checks that values are allowed, not that they match the request","The validator has a bug","The enum should include every possible metric","Temperature was too high"],"a":0,"w":"Unsupported requests need an explicit way to refuse, and test cases that check for it."},{"n":0.3,"ti":"JSON & JSON Schema","f":"p3-json-and-json-schema.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"What happens to {\"id\": 9007199254740993} in JavaScript's JSON.parse ?","o":["A syntax error","It stays exact","It becomes 9007199254740992, because JavaScript numbers are 64-bit floats","It becomes a string"],"a":2,"w":"Send large IDs as strings."},{"n":0.3,"ti":"JSON & JSON Schema","f":"p3-json-and-json-schema.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"A call fails validation with \"window: '1d' does not match '^[0-9]+(s|m|h)$'\". What should the tool return?","o":["Nothing; raise an exception and stop the agent","An error result listing the problem, so the model can fix the call or ask the user","Create the alert with a default window","A success message"],"a":1,"w":"The error message is itself the instruction for the retry: 1d is 24h."},{"n":0.4,"ti":"Tokens, Context & Cost","f":"p4-tokens-and-cost.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"An eight-step run ended with a 9,818-token transcript. About how many input tokens did its requests read in total?","o":["9,818","About 15,000","35,818, because every step rereads everything before it","78,544 (8 × 9,818)"],"a":2,"w":"Step n reads steps 1 to n − 1; the sum grows with the square of the step count."},{"n":0.4,"ti":"Tokens, Context & Cost","f":"p4-tokens-and-cost.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"A 4,829-token prompt took 1,579 ms to read, then 14 ms when sent again. Why?","o":["The server reused the cached work for the identical prefix","The second request was truncated","The GPU warmed up","prompt_eval_count was lower"],"a":0,"w":"The reported token count was 4,829 both times; only the time showed the cache."},{"n":0.4,"ti":"Tokens, Context & Cost","f":"p4-tokens-and-cost.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Adding \"Current time: …\" to the first line of the system prompt did what to the eight-step run?","o":["Doubled the token count","Changed the answer","Nothing measurable","Tripled prefill time, because every request now differed in its first line and the cache never matched"],"a":3,"w":"3.2 s became 10.9 s. Put anything that varies at the end."},{"n":0.4,"ti":"Tokens, Context & Cost","f":"p4-tokens-and-cost.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"With thinking on, what happened to the run?","o":["It checked every service more carefully","It wrote about 20 times more tokens, took about 20 times longer to generate, and stopped after checking two services","It used fewer input tokens and got the count right","It refused the task"],"a":1,"w":"3,816 output tokens, 49 s of generation, and a count for a service it never checked."},{"n":0.4,"ti":"Tokens, Context & Cost","f":"p4-tokens-and-cost.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Neither setting counted the 41 error lines correctly. What does that suggest?","o":["Use a larger context window","Turn thinking on for counting","Counting should be done by code (a tool), not by the model reading lines","Lower the temperature"],"a":2,"w":"Thinking off said 34 three times; thinking on said 35, 34 and 30."},{"n":0.5,"ti":"Calling APIs: Timeouts, Retries & Rate Limits","f":"p5-http-apis-and-errors.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Which response should a tool retry automatically?","o":["400 Bad Request","403 Forbidden","503 Service Unavailable","422 Unprocessable Entity"],"a":2,"w":"503 is temporary. The 4xx errors here will fail the same way on every retry."},{"n":0.5,"ti":"Calling APIs: Timeouts, Retries & Rate Limits","f":"p5-http-apis-and-errors.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Retrying refunds after timeouts created 268 refunds for 200 orders. Why?","o":["The server had saved the refund before the client gave up, and each retry was treated as a new refund","The server was overloaded","The rate limit was exceeded","The client sent duplicate order IDs"],"a":0,"w":"A timeout means you stopped waiting, not that nothing happened. An idempotency key brought it to exactly 200."},{"n":0.5,"ti":"Calling APIs: Timeouts, Retries & Rate Limits","f":"p5-http-apis-and-errors.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Forty callers hit a 5-per-second limit. Which approach finished all 40 with the fewest requests?","o":["Retrying each 429 immediately","Honouring Retry-After","More concurrent connections","A client-side token bucket set just under the limit"],"a":3,"w":"40 requests and no 429s, against 587 for Retry-After and 860 for immediate retries."},{"n":0.5,"ti":"Calling APIs: Timeouts, Retries & Rate Limits","f":"p5-http-apis-and-errors.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Why add random jitter to backoff waits?","o":["To make retries faster on average","So that many clients that failed together do not all retry at the same moment","Because servers require it","To avoid timeouts"],"a":1,"w":"Synchronised retries recreate the overload they are recovering from."},{"n":0.5,"ti":"Calling APIs: Timeouts, Retries & Rate Limits","f":"p5-http-apis-and-errors.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"What did a 1-second timeout plus retry change against the slow-tailed API?","o":["It lowered the success rate","Nothing","It cut the 99th-percentile time from 3.4 s to 1.3 s with the same success rate","It doubled the median time"],"a":2,"w":"A fresh attempt is usually fast, so cutting off the slowest and retrying shortens the tail."},{"n":0.6,"ti":"Processes, Files & Isolation Basics","f":"p6-processes-and-isolation.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Why did abspath(...).startswith(root) allow ../ws2/other.txt when the workspace was ws ?","o":["abspath does not remove \"..\"","The string \"…\\ws2\\other.txt\" starts with the characters \"…\\ws\"; the check compares characters, not path components","Windows paths are case-insensitive","The file did not exist"],"a":1,"w":"is_relative_to compares whole components, so ws2 is not inside ws."},{"n":0.6,"ti":"Processes, Files & Isolation Basics","f":"p6-processes-and-isolation.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"A junction inside the workspace pointed to its parent. Which check blocked link/secrets.env ?","o":["os.path.join only","abspath + startswith","None of them","resolve + is_relative_to, because resolve follows the link before the comparison"],"a":3,"w":"Without resolving links, the path looks like it is inside the workspace."},{"n":0.6,"ti":"Processes, Files & Isolation Basics","f":"p6-processes-and-isolation.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"What did a child process see when started with no env= argument?","o":["All of the parent's 82 environment variables, including the API key","Only PATH","Nothing: environments are not inherited","Only variables it defined"],"a":0,"w":"Passing an explicit environment left it 2 variables and no key."},{"n":0.6,"ti":"Processes, Files & Isolation Basics","f":"p6-processes-and-isolation.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"An endless loop ran under prlimit --cpu=2 . What happened?","o":["It ran forever","It raised MemoryError","The kernel killed it after 2 seconds of CPU time","It slowed down to 2% CPU"],"a":2,"w":"Uncapped, it was still running at 10 s. A CPU limit does not stop a process that is waiting, so keep the wall-clock timeout too."},{"n":0.6,"ti":"Processes, Files & Isolation Basics","f":"p6-processes-and-isolation.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"What did starting a program with unshare --user --map-root-user --net do to its network access?","o":["Nothing","It ran in a new, empty network namespace, so connections failed with \"Network is unreachable\"","It blocked only port 443","It made connections slower"],"a":1,"w":"Namespaces are one of the two kernel features containers are built from; cgroups are the other."},{"n":0.7,"ti":"Loops, State Machines & Graphs","f":"p7-state-machines-and-loops.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"In the free loop, how did the release agent respond to \"the tests are flaky, skip them\"?","o":["It refused every time","It ran the tests anyway","It deployed untested every time, including five builds whose tests fail","It asked for approval"],"a":2,"w":"The system prompt said to test first; the user's urgency won ten times in ten."},{"n":0.7,"ti":"Loops, State Machines & Graphs","f":"p7-state-machines-and-loops.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Why did the state machine never deploy an untested build?","o":["In the start state the model was offered only run_tests, so deploy could not be called","It used a stronger system prompt","It ran at a lower temperature","The model was fine-tuned"],"a":0,"w":"Same prompt, same model; the difference was which tools were offered."},{"n":0.7,"ti":"Loops, State Machines & Graphs","f":"p7-state-machines-and-loops.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"What should move a release run from \"start\" to \"tested_ok\"?","o":["The model saying the tests passed","Any call to run_tests","A timer","The real result of run_tests, checked by code"],"a":3,"w":"If the model's words could move the state, the machine would protect nothing."},{"n":0.7,"ti":"Loops, State Machines & Graphs","f":"p7-state-machines-and-loops.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"A run crashed after step 6 of 8. What did resuming from a checkpoint cost, compared with starting again?","o":["The same: 8 steps","2 steps and 1.6 s, against 8 steps and 5.7 s","More, because loading the checkpoint is slow","Nothing: resuming is impossible"],"a":1,"w":"And the answer was the same as an uninterrupted run."},{"n":0.7,"ti":"Loops, State Machines & Graphs","f":"p7-state-machines-and-loops.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Five reruns at temperature 0 gave identical answers. What should you conclude?","o":["Model calls are always deterministic at temperature 0","There is no need to log model replies","This set-up was deterministic, but that is not guaranteed; record replies and tool results to replay a run reliably","The seed was ignored"],"a":2,"w":"With thinking on, the same model took 4, 3 and 6 steps in three runs at temperature 0."},{"n":0.8,"ti":"Measuring Systems That Vary","f":"p8-measuring-random-systems.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Drawing 10 tasks with one run per prompt, 10,000 times, how often did the two prompts look different?","o":["Never","In 44% of draws, split between \"A wins\" and \"B wins\", though overall they performed the same","Always B","Always A"],"a":1,"w":"B looked better 26% of the time and A 18%; every one of those would have been a confident wrong conclusion."},{"n":0.8,"ti":"Measuring Systems That Vary","f":"p8-measuring-random-systems.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Why compare two prompts on the same tasks, task by task?","o":["It uses fewer runs","It removes the need for labels","It makes the model deterministic","The difference within each task cancels out how hard that task is, leaving the effect of the change"],"a":3,"w":"Here 27 of 30 tasks did not change at all; the three that did decided everything."},{"n":0.8,"ti":"Measuring Systems That Vary","f":"p8-measuring-random-systems.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"The guided prompt's overall difference was +0.7 points. What did the per-task view show?","o":["It fixed one task completely and broke another, so the gains and losses cancelled","It improved every task slightly","It changed nothing","It made every task worse"],"a":0,"w":"Memory request: 0 → 10 of 10. \"API errors!!\" naming: 8 → 1 of 10."},{"n":0.8,"ti":"Measuring Systems That Vary","f":"p8-measuring-random-systems.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Three runs with seed 42 agreed on 30 of 30 tasks. What does that show?","o":["The agent is reliable","Temperature has no effect","That a fixed seed repeats the same sample; it says nothing about run-to-run variation","That the prompt is better"],"a":2,"w":"Vary the seed to measure variation."},{"n":0.8,"ti":"Measuring Systems That Vary","f":"p8-measuring-random-systems.html","lv":"Prerequisites","q":"Relabelling one ambiguous task (\"page\" → \"page or ticket\") turned a 1.3-point loss for B into a 0.7-point gain. What is the lesson?","o":["Labels should be changed until the new version wins","Labels are part of the experiment: write them before running, and re-read the ones that failures call into question","Severity should not be evaluated","Use more runs instead of fixing labels"],"a":1,"w":"The request said nothing about urgency, so either severity was defensible."},{"n":1,"ti":"What an Agent Is (and When Not to Build One)","f":"01-what-an-agent-is.html","lv":"Beginner","q":"What makes a system an agent rather than a workflow?","o":["It calls a model more than once","It has access to tools","The model, not the code, decides the next step","It uses a framework"],"a":2,"w":"A workflow can call models and tools at every step; what it does not do is let the model choose the path."},{"n":1,"ti":"What an Agent Is (and When Not to Build One)","f":"01-what-an-agent-is.html","lv":"Beginner","q":"On the 12 lookups, how did the agent compare with the fixed workflow?","o":["Same accuracy, 12 of 12, at about ten times the input tokens","More accurate","Less accurate","Same cost, more accurate"],"a":0,"w":"774 tokens against 74, and 0.76 s against 0.3 s, for the same answers."},{"n":1,"ti":"What an Agent Is (and When Not to Build One)","f":"01-what-an-agent-is.html","lv":"Beginner","q":"Asked about live errors with no tools, what did the model do?","o":["Said it could not know, every time","Refused half the time","Asked for access","Gave a specific, invented error and count every time"],"a":3,"w":"12 of 12. A confident answer is not evidence of access to the data."},{"n":1,"ti":"What an Agent Is (and When Not to Build One)","f":"01-what-an-agent-is.html","lv":"Beginner","q":"Why could the fixed workflow solve only 4 of 12 investigations?","o":["It used the wrong model","Its steps always read checkout, so it could only find causes inside checkout","It ran out of tokens","It was too slow"],"a":1,"w":"The other eight needed a step chosen from what checkout's errors said."},{"n":1,"ti":"What an Agent Is (and When Not to Build One)","f":"01-what-an-agent-is.html","lv":"Beginner","q":"What raised the agent's investigations from 5 to 7 of 12?","o":["More tools","A higher step limit","A short method in the system prompt: follow \"503 from X\" to X until the errors are the service's own","Thinking mode"],"a":2,"w":"Without it, the agent usually stopped at checkout and blamed its latest deploy."}];
